version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-kernel-setup
description: >-
  First-run setup on the kernel side: the setup endpoint the GUI walks through
  (setup-endpoint.ts) and the preflight checks it runs before provisioning
  (preflight.ts).
context:
  - >-
    The $first-run flow and the ^setup-token gate stay in
    packages/gnomon/.purpose.
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  setup-endpoint:
    description: >-
      #setup-endpoint (spec §11.2 rule 11, §2.4 rule 9; T-2026-10-19-005
      MVP-b) — the SETUP MODE loopback endpoint: a #web-endpoint (same
      gnomon-web transport child, rules.ts, 127.0.0.1 only, the SAME pinned
      #gui bundle) whose dispatcher is the closed gnomon-setup:v1 protocol
      (gnomon-contracts setup.ts, own SETUP_API_ID; clientApiId unchanged):
      hello / auth {setupToken} / setup.preflight / setup.name / setup.begin /
      setup.purge {gen} / setup.complete (I10, the saved row, 0 prompts) /
      setup.finish, events setup.state and setup.presence
      {n,of,purpose,digest12}. No gnomon-rpc verb is reachable. An ephemeral
      Ed25519 setup key signs serverSig. One setup connection; a closed
      socket aborts the #provisioner at its next step boundary. Exact params
      key sets: the page carries only name, a server-listed gen, and clicks.
      Entry: bare gnomon / gnomon setup on a TTY print the setup URL (and
      every expected digest: the terminal is the surface to trust); gnomon
      setup --cli keeps the prompts; up --wrapper emits {t:setup,...} and then
      continues into {t:up}. Falsified in test/setup-endpoint.test.ts
      (G-SET-08..14) and test/wrapper-channel.test.ts. Never hangs: it
      settles on finish (also for an already-set-up home), token expiry, a
      10 min idle cap, socket close, transport stop or token reuse; a refused
      purge (GNOMON_HOME guard, in-use / identity-malformed) or a failed
      begin returns to the checks. The checks are read-only: setup state
      lives in a private scratch dir and the home is created at begin.
      stop() removes that scratch dir BEFORE it waits for a running step, so
      the wrapper's quit / stdin EOF (Gnomon.app Cmd-Q, which kills the
      kernel at most 10 s later) cleans it even with a Touch ID prompt held
      open; an EOF that came before waitSetup listened also stops it. A
      failed rm (e.g. EACCES) never rejects stop(); the next run sweeps it.
    path: src/kernel/setup/setup-endpoint.ts
    type: service
    related: ["#provisioner", "#setup-preflight", "#web-endpoint", "#gui-setup", "#first-run"]
    tests:
      - test/setup-endpoint.test.ts
      - test/wrapper-channel.test.ts
    gates: ["^setup-token", "^unprovisioned-only"]
    tags: [kernel, setup, web]
  setup-preflight:
    description: >-
      #setup-preflight (spec §2.4 rule 9) — READ-ONLY first-run checks (no
      key, no file write, no prompt; only key.list): helper signed+pinned and
      not from a sandboxed shell, touch-id (helper 1.4.0 presence.available:
      LAContext canEvaluatePolicy, never a prompt; pass or fail), macos (floor 15 =
      SESSION_SANDBOX_MIN_MACOS, TD-2026-10-22-220: below it fails naming the update,
      matching the app's LSMinimumSystemVersion and the helper/voice-io targets;
      test/macos-floor.test.ts pins them), sip (csrutil;
      off = warn), claude (resolved, pin none/match/mismatch → `gnomon session
      repin-claude`), law-7 billing env, runtime (NODE_OPTIONS / node flags),
      node floor (NODE_MAJOR_FLOOR 24, equal to scripts/install-darwin.mjs: the
      source-install floor; a zero-build release bundles its own Node),
      leftover generations (purge, never adopt), home state (dev
      marker, symlink, malformed identity.json: shown, never touched). Each
      check {id, status pass|warn|fail, detail, fix}. INFORMATIVE only (Aegis
      I12): #provisioner and #gnomon-up enforce on their own. The helper row
      names the build's #release-pins mode (release sha256-pinned, or dev).
    path: src/kernel/setup/preflight.ts
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, kernel, setup]
    related: ["#first-run", "#provisioner"]
    tests:
      - test/setup.test.ts
